openFPGALoader is a universal utility for programming FPGAs and their
attached SPI flash. It supports devices from Xilinx, Altera/Intel,
Lattice, Gowin, Efinix, Anlogic, Cologne Chip and others, through a
wide range of JTAG/SPI cables (FTDI-based, DirtyJTAG, USB-Blaster I/II,
CMSIS-DAP, J-Link, CH347, DFU, Xilinx Virtual Cable, remote bitbang...).

A udev rule (/lib/udev/rules.d/99-openfpgaloader.rules) is installed
that gives the "plugdev" group access to supported cables. To use
openFPGALoader as a normal user, add yourself to that group:

  usermod -a -G plugdev <username>

then log out and back in. The alternative rule 70-openfpgaloader.rules
(uaccess only, no group) is included in the doc directory.

Required dependencies (SBo):
  libftdi1 - FTDI-based cables, USB-Blaster I, XVC server, and
             CologneChip/Efinix/iCE40/Lattice SSPI support
  hidapi   - CMSIS-DAP v1 support
libusb, eudev (libudev) and zlib come with Slackware itself.

Optional dependency, auto-detected at build time:
  libgpiod - enables the libgpiod bitbang driver (pass GPIOD=no to
             disable it even if installed)

hidapi is needed for CMSIS-DAP v1 support. To build without it, pass
CMSISDAP_V1=no to the script.
